{"chunk_id": "c-f7ebe6e72a67cb30", "claim_id": "A034-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A034", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "When you use the Shamir seal with multiple nodes, you must unseal each node with the required threshold of shares. Vault does not distribute partially unsealed nodes across the cluster.", "span_end": 2213, "span_start": 2028, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-355b02bf3ff04cd1", "claim_id": "A034-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/integrated-storage", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A034", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "When using Shamir seal, the joined nodes will still need to be unsealed", "span_end": 3544, "span_start": 3473, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-f7ebe6e72a67cb30", "claim_id": "A036-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "If there is a detected intrusion, you can seal the Vault data quickly to try to minimize damages.", "span_end": 3000, "span_start": 2903, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-f7ebe6e72a67cb30", "claim_id": "A036-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Users cannot access the data from a sealed Vault without access to the root key shares.", "span_end": 3088, "span_start": 3001, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-26212d3706d4a4a2", "claim_id": "A036-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Sealing tells the Vault server to stop responding to any operations until it is unsealed. When sealed, the Vault server discards its in-memory root key to unlock the data, so it is physically blocked from responding to operations unsealed.", "span_end": 300, "span_start": 61, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-b0c512b6155a9b42", "claim_id": "A037-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/configuration/prevent-lease-explosions", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Unchecked lease explosions create a memory drain on the active node, which can cascade to other nodes and result in denial-of-service issues for the entire cluster.", "span_end": 438, "span_start": 274, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-bcb8d40555aaacec", "claim_id": "A037-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/tune-server-performance", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "These leases represent a commitment to do future work in the form of revocation, which involves connecting to external hosts to revoke the credential there as well. In addition, Vault has internal maintenance to perform in the form of deleting (potentially recursively) expired tokens and leases.", "span_end": 1823, "span_start": 1527, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-b3550b8e9e5d0aa2", "claim_id": "A037-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/limits", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Although no technical maximum exists, high lease counts can cause degradation in system performance. We recommend short default time-to-live values on tokens and leases to avoid a large backlog of unexpired leases, or a large number of simultaneous expirations.", "span_end": 745, "span_start": 484, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-947a97ed02c3f755", "claim_id": "A038-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/transform", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A038", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Vault transform creates a new key for each tokenization transformation, which\nhelps ensure a strong cryptographic distinction between different tokenization\nuse cases.", "span_end": 349, "span_start": 182, "supported": true}
